= Agent initialization — Simple =

'''Agent initialization''' is what happens before an AI agent begins its normal work.

A simple agent may only need to load settings.

A persistent agent may also need to determine:

* which agent it is;
* which memories belong to it;
* which goals and rules are current;
* which permissions it has;
* which tools are available;
* whether old state is still valid.

A restart is not always the same as a fresh start. A resumed agent may need to restore earlier state, while a new agent may need a new identity and empty state.

Initialization matters because a mistake at the beginning can affect every later step.

